<p>China said President Trump will make a state visit to Beijing from May 13 to 15 at President Xi Jinping&#x27;s invitation, the first visit to China by a U.S. president since Trump&#x27;s 2017 trip. U.S. officials said the leaders are expected to discuss trade tensions, Iran, Taiwan, artificial intelligence, nuclear weapons and critical minerals in their first face-to-face talks in more than six months. The visit had been planned for late March or early April but was postponed as Trump focused on the Iran war. U.S. officials said Trump would press Xi on Iran, including China&#x27;s purchases of Iranian oil, while seeking steps to ease economic disputes between the world&#x27;s two largest economies.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/1Kovq1ItG7IhZTpZKRGN7DewH0XxFKliApzmVWBqlgm6NURlW-e1zcm8WKmJShrA7B1IBgkATas6emnIzPU4fMH5RTMUYgHdVU63ipYYkLKigNqZe57WBQyPXXd1c4QkMt4yYxWm6pLvPl15j9oMWMEYMhGdciRF_WcQQeB9Vm_BDFhcdzSm8eB73izsoWWNjogyMNkU7LUWI3sDAXdrwYOBF9Q2ksxXJGVHkiOx3ZQ2kGMV_kuWCqksjhbS006exiHWdwBYr1GeKXwcAQ' alt='President Donald Trump and Chinese President Xi Jinping participate in a welcome ceremony at the Great Hall of the People in Beijing, China, Nov. 9, 2017.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Trade forums: U.S. officials said Washington and Beijing may announce a Board of Trade and a Board of Investment, though the mechanisms would need further work before implementation.</li><li>Commercial purchases: U.S. officials previewing the talks said China is expected to announce purchases related to Boeing airplanes, American agriculture and energy.</li><li>Minerals truce: The two sides are weighing an extension of a trade-war truce that allows rare earth minerals to continue flowing from China to the United States.</li><li>Beijing itinerary: The White House said Trump is scheduled for a welcome ceremony, a bilateral meeting, a Temple of Heaven visit, a state banquet, tea and a working lunch before returning to Washington.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>W